            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0893" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 K 55/129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Advise Nansen of substance of Riga’s No. 444, June 21, which Riga is
                    repeating to you and inquire if Nansen has made any progress toward release of
                    Americans.</p>
                <p>Let him know that situation reported by Riga is regarded by this Government as
                    most serious and that consideration is being given to every possible means of
                    terminating it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
